{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "label": "idempotent middleware", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Enforces at-most-once write processing: the handler runs only on the first request and subsequent requests with the same key replay the stored response, so a network retry cannot double-charge."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotencyoptions", "label": "IdempotencyOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "keyPrefix defaults to idem: so multiple wrappers in one Redis do not collide; missingHeader defaults to reject, with pass-through for fleets where only some clients send the header."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotency_key_header", "label": "Idempotency-Key header", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client must mint the key once before the first attempt and reuse it on retry; generating one inside the retry loop is the common bug that defeats the whole mechanism."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_request_fingerprint", "label": "SHA-256 request fingerprint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Method, path, query and body are stored alongside each cached response; a same-key request differing in any of them is rejected with 422, so a client cannot reuse a key for a semantically different request to receive the wrong stored response."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_canonical_query_folding", "label": "Canonical query folding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parameter keys are sorted so a reordered retry still replays \u2014 reordering is not a different request \u2014 but the values of a repeated key keep their original order, which matters for any API that reads such a list positionally."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_key_validation", "label": "Key validation (length and control characters)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The header value is attacker-chosen and lands verbatim in a cache key: CR and LF are the classic header-injection pair, and space plus the control range are command delimiters in Memcached text protocol, so a key carrying one is only safe depending on which Cache is wired in behind the middleware. The rejection names the limit and the offending index, never the key itself."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_identity_scope", "label": "identity scope and maxScopeLength", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Folds a per-caller scope into the cache key so an identity-specific response is never replayed to a different caller (security audit HTTP-4). Both key rules apply to it, because it is the other half of the same composed key \u2014 a two-character key with a 64 KiB x-account header used to be accepted. Two separate caps rather than one over the composed key, so a tenant with a long id cannot spend an honest client header budget."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_in_flight_409", "label": "In-flight claim returns 409 Conflict", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second concurrent request is refused immediately rather than queued. Failing fast instead of holding the connection open for the handler runtime also means there is no cross-pod lock to coordinate \u2014 the in-flight marker lives in the same cache as the responses."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_cached_response", "label": "The complete response is stored", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A returned response is cached unconditionally, 4xx and 5xx included, so a payment-failed reply is not re-processed into a payment-succeeded; a handler that throws instead drops its in-flight claim, leaving the key free to retry."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_rediscache_multipod", "label": "RedisCache for multi-pod deployments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "InMemoryCache is per-pod state, so a retry landing on a different pod re-processes."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_inmemorycache_eviction", "label": "InMemoryCache eviction hazards", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three silent failure modes even with guarantee-aware eviction: a flood of rate-limit counters evicts records because the policy does not rank guarantees against each other; this middleware own key space is attacker-controlled, so a flood of distinct keys evicts other callers records; and a record is only marked most-recently-used when read, so setIfAbsent leaves a claimed-but-unretried key first to be dropped."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_ttl_loss", "label": "Cache loss equals double processing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After the TTL the key is forgotten and a delayed retry processes again \u2014 pick a TTL longer than any reasonable retry window, 24 hours being typical for payments."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotencyoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotency_key_header", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotency_key_header", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_key_validation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_key_validation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_identity_scope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_request_fingerprint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_request_fingerprint", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_canonical_query_folding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_cached_response", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_in_flight_409", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotencyoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_ttl_loss", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotencyoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_rediscache_multipod", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_rediscache_multipod", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_inmemorycache_eviction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_inmemorycache_eviction", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_cache_isolation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_idempotent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_effectively_once", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_request_fingerprint", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_producer_incarnation", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_idempotency_key_cached_response", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_dedup_triple", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/idempotency-key.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}